Bug fix: align hit detection with visual enemy position — all maps.

This commit modifies 5 files (+331/-28 lines), spanning 2 core game loop, 1 networking, 1 tests.
This fix addresses a reported bug or regression in the game. Bug fixes in this project follow the TDD protocol: a failing test was written first to reproduce the issue, then the fix was applied to make the test pass, ensuring the defect cannot silently regress.

Additional context from the commit body:
CollisionSystem, GameInstance, and network-main.ts now use
enemy.mesh.position (visual, elevated above surface by normal*radius)
instead of enemy.position (on-surface) for collision checks. Hit radius
inflated to 2*radius² to account for the perpendicular offset from
bullet plane to elevated enemy center.

Files touched: CollisionSystem.ts (SP), network-main.ts (MP),
GameInstance.ts (playground), regression test.

Game state: SP all maps working. Hit detection was offset by ~1 enemy
body width on curved surfaces (Mobius, torus, peanut) due to parallax
between surface-level collision and elevated visual rendering.

